sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant UI as Kibana Workflow UI
    participant Identity as Kibana Execution Identity
    participant Security as Kibana Security UIAM Client
    participant ESO as Encrypted Saved Objects
    participant UIAM
    participant Engine as Workflow Management / Engine
    participant ES as Elasticsearch / CPS Projects

    Note over User,UIAM: 1. Create a service account
    User->>UI: Choose projects
    UI->>Security: delegableRoles(projects, custom role candidates)
    Security->>UIAM: POST /api-keys/_delegable_roles
    UIAM-->>UI: Covered built-in and custom roles
    User->>UI: Choose roles and optional trusted caller roles
    UI->>Identity: Create execution identity
    Identity->>Security: grantApiKey(projectRoleAssignments, allowedRoleAssignments)
    Security->>UIAM: POST /api-keys/_grant with assignments and use policy
    UIAM-->>Security: Downscoped UIAM API key
    Identity->>ESO: Encrypt key and save space-scoped identity
    Identity-->>UI: Service account UUID

    Note over User,UIAM: 2. Open or edit a workflow with settings.run_as
    UI->>Identity: getForDisplay(UUID)
    Identity-->>UI: Name, roles, and projects
    UI->>Identity: canUse(UUID)
    Identity->>Security: canUse(apiKeyId)
    Security->>UIAM: POST /api-keys/{id}/_can_use
    UIAM->>UIAM: Check organization admin, role trust policy, or role containment
    UIAM-->>Security: Allowed or denied
    Security-->>Identity: Authorization result
    Identity-->>UI: Authorization result
    Note right of UI: Denied means read-only workflow and disabled Run/Save

    Note over User,ES: 3. Execute an allowed workflow
    User->>UI: Run workflow
    UI->>Engine: Execute with run_as UUID
    Engine->>Identity: Re-check canUse and resolve credential
    Identity->>ESO: Decrypt UIAM API key
    Identity-->>Engine: Scoped execution request
    Engine->>ES: API key plus project_routing
    ES-->>Engine: Results from authorized projects only
    Engine-->>UI: Execution result and service-account audit metadata

    Note over Engine,UIAM: 4. Nested service-account switch
    Engine->>Engine: Child workflow declares a different run_as UUID
    Engine->>Identity: canUse(child UUID) with parent API-key request
    Identity->>UIAM: POST /api-keys/{childKeyId}/_can_use
    UIAM->>UIAM: Check parent key roles against child trust policy
    UIAM-->>Engine: Allow or deny identity switch
    Engine->>Identity: Resolve child credential only when allowed

    Note over User,ES: Known PoC boundary
    Note over UIAM,ES: Runtime authentication sees the API key, not the human actor or workflow binding

    Note over User,ES: Long-term native UIAM service account
    User->>UIAM: Bind native service account to workflow
    UIAM-->>Engine: Actor and workload-scoped binding capability
    Engine->>UIAM: Exchange capability at execution time
    UIAM->>UIAM: Re-evaluate policy and revocation
    UIAM-->>Engine: Short-lived execution credential
    Engine->>ES: Execute with short-lived credential
